description:
Design a simple arithmetic logic unit (ALU) that performs basic operations based on a 3-bit operation code. When the operation code is set to '001', the ALU outputs the sum of two 16-bit inputs (in1 and in2). When the operation code is '010', the ALU simply outputs the first 16-bit input (in1). For any other operation code, the output is undefined (1'bX).
module top_module(
  input wire[15:0] in1, in2,
  input wire[2:0]alu_op,  
  output reg[15:0] Z
);

code:
module top_module(
  input wire[15:0] in1, in2,
  input wire[2:0]alu_op,  
  output reg[15:0] Z
);always@* begin
    if(alu_op==3'b001) 
      Z = in1+in2;
    else if(alu_op==3'b010) 
      Z = in1;
    else
      Z = 1'bX;
  end

endmodule

